Description: the default of num_history_items_recorded, the one limit of every history list of mc (the command line, the directories of each panel, the input fields), is 1000 instead of 60
Origin: azsupport/ports (aZ, 12.11.2026: 1000 lines by default are enough)
Why: 60 entries of the command line and of the directories of a panel are few for a
 server. An existing ~/.config/mc/ini keeps its value: with auto_save_setup (on by
 default) mc writes num_history_items_recorded=60 into it at its exit, so on a server
 that already has one it is changed there (or the line removed).

--- lib/mcconfig/history.c.orig
+++ lib/mcconfig/history.c
@@ -47,8 +47,9 @@
 
 /*** global variables ****************************************************************************/
 
-/* how much history items are used */
-int num_history_items_recorded = 60;
+/* how much history items are used (the default of num_history_items_recorded in the ini:
+ * 1000 in the mc of azsupport/ports, 60 in mc) */
+int num_history_items_recorded = 1000;
 
 /*** file scope macro definitions ****************************************************************/
 
